UPDATE characters SET data = '{"slug":"duende","name":"Duende","team":"outsider","ability":"You start knowing a question. Each day or night*, privately answer it: if correct, you see the Grimoire & turn evil.","creator":"legitch","appearsIn":"SCP Fragmented Veil","lede":"The Duende scavenges for things to steal, and - if crafty - uncovers the booty of the Grimoire.","summaryBullets":["The Duende starts knowing a question, and nothing else. Should they correctly answer it, they gain the benefit of seeing into the Grimoire, and becoming evil.","Nothing bad happens to the good team should the Duende fail to answer their question at all whilst they live.","It is Duende''s choice to answer their question, should they decide they want to remain good and not risk being evil.","The Duende can answer once per day, or night. They only wake at night to answer if they didn''t do so during the day, and the type of question they have can permit a silent answer during the night.","The Duende effectively knows if they are incorrect in their answer, since they won''t plunder any rewards on failure {{i|(unless drunk or poisoned)}}.","Jinxes involving the Duende seeing into the Grimoire should be less severe against them."],"howToRun":["During setup, write a question on a piece of paper, or on a phone.","During the first night, wake the Duende. Show this question, then put them to sleep.","Once per day, if the Duende requests a private chat with you, take them away from the circle so you cannot be overheard. They give their answer. If incorrect, mark them with the **INCORRECT** reminder token.","Each night except the first, if the Duende''s question or the game''s medium permits them to answer silently during the night and they are not marked with the **INCORRECT** reminder token, wake them. Show them the question again, then they give the signals necessary to answer it. Afterwards, put them to sleep.","Each dawn, remove the **INCORRECT** reminder token if its present.","If the Duende answers correctly, jackpot! Show them the ' || char(8220) || 'You Are' || char(8221) || ' info token, and a thumbs down. Show them the Grimoire for as long as they need."],"tips":["The Duende should generally be given a question that can only leave them with a 5% to 10% or less chance of guessing successfully if going by random chance alone and nothing else."],"quote":"> wife pregnant for 8 months\n> her water breaks, rush her to hospital\n> she goes into intensive labour & passes away due to complications\n> doctor hands me what came out of womb\n> 2 gold ' || char(214) || 'rtugs, a dead chicken, and 1 I.O.U\n> fucking duendes","iconBy":"Game-icons.net","jinxes":[{"name":"Damsel","align":"good","text":"When the Duende correctly answers their question, they may choose to only learn the evil players & their characters instead of the whole Grimoire. If not, the Damsel is poisoned.","id":"damsel"},{"name":"Heretic","align":"good","text":"When the Duende correctly answers their question, they may choose to only learn the evil players & their characters instead of the whole Grimoire. If not, the Heretic is poisoned.","id":"heretic"},{"name":"Abdominal","align":"good","text":"Only 1 jinxed character can be in play.","slug":"abdominal"},{"name":"xX_2662_Xx","align":"evil","text":"Instead of adding 1 Outsider, 1 Townsfolk is secretly drunk. When the Duende views the Grimoire, they see xX_2662_Xx as the Demon whose ability they have and doesn''t know who is secretly drunk.","slug":"xx-2662-xx"},{"name":"Wig Snatcher","align":"good","text":"The Wig Snatcher cannot become the Duende.","id":"wigsnatcher_hblreleased"},{"name":"Au' || char(8217) || 'Wre","align":"evil","text":"If Au' || char(8217) || 'Wre is in play, the Duende only sees half of the Grimoire.","id":"auwre_the_bootleggers_anthology"},{"name":"Ketos","align":"evil","text":"If Ketos is in play, the Duende learns all in-play characters & evil players instead of seeing the Grimoire.","id":"ketos_the_bootleggers_anthology"},{"name":"Visionary","align":"evil","text":"When the Duende correctly answers their question, they may choose to only learn the evil players & their characters instead of the whole Grimoire. If not, the Visionary is poisoned.","id":"visionary_the_bootleggers_anthology"}],"customBoxes":[{"title":"Credit","content":"Ability: @legitch. Image: Game-icons.net"},{"title":"Alternative JSON & How to Run (Older)","content":"If you want to use the older version of the Duende, where it also transformed into a Minion upon a correct answer of their question, use this JSON. Arguably much stronger and detrimental the good team upon their transformation, use at your own risk.\n\nDuring setup, write a question on a piece of paper, or on a phone.\n\nDuring the first night, wake the Duende. Show this question, then put them to sleep.\n\nOnce per day, if the Duende requests a private chat with you, take them away from the circle so you cannot be overheard. They give their answer. If incorrect, mark them with the **INCORRECT** reminder token.\n\nEach night except the first, if the Duende''s question or the game''s medium permits them to answer silently during the night and they are not marked with the **INCORRECT** reminder token, wake them. Show them the question again, then they give the signals necessary to answer it. Afterwards, put them to sleep.\n\nEach dawn, remove the **INCORRECT** reminder token if its present.\n\nIf the Duende answers correctly, jackpot! Replace their old character token with a Minion token, show them the ' || char(8220) || 'You Are' || char(8221) || ' info token then the Minion character token, and give a thumbs down. Show them the Grimoire for as long as they need.\n\nIf the Duende transforms into an evil Minion already in-play and you don''t have duplicate character tokens for this Minion, you may instead flip the Duende''s character token upside-down {{i|(to indicate to yourself that they are evil)}} and mark the current Minion with the **USES MINION OF** reminder, to indicate that they are effectively this Minion. Use the Duende''s **?** reminders if needed, to substitute for the Minion''s own reminders.\n\n**Duende ' || char(9608) || '+** (Outsider)\nYou start knowing a question. Each day or night*, privately answer it: if correct, you see the Grimoire & become an evil Minion.\n\n**First night:** Show the Duende their question.\n**Other nights:** You may show the Duende their question if it can be answered tonight. The Duende shows the signals needed to answer it. If correct, change their token to a Minion token. Show them the ''You Are'' card, the Minions they have become, a thumbs down, and then the Grimoire for as long as they need.\n**Reminders:** Incorrect, Uses Minion of, ?, ?, ?\n**Credit:** Ability: @legitch. Image: Game-icons.net\n\n**Jinxes:**\nDamsel: When the Duende correctly answers their question, they may choose to only learn the evil players & their characters instead of the whole Grimoire. If not, the Damsel is poisoned.\nHeretic: When the Duende correctly answers their question, they may choose to only learn the evil players & their characters instead of the whole Grimoire. If not, the Heretic is poisoned.\nAbdominal: Only 1 jinxed character can be in play.\nxX_2662_Xx: Instead of adding 1 Outsider, 1 Townsfolk is secretly drunk. When the Duende views the Grimoire, they see xX_2662_Xx as the Demon whose ability they have and doesn''t know who is secretly drunk.\nWig Snatcher: The Wig Snatcher cannot become the Duende.\nAu' || char(8217) || 'Wre: If Au' || char(8217) || 'Wre is in play, the Duende only sees half of the Grimoire.\nKetos: If Ketos is in play, the Duende learns all in-play characters & evil players instead of seeing the Grimoire.\nVisionary: When the Duende correctly answers their question, they may choose to only learn the evil players & their characters instead of the whole Grimoire. If not, the Visionary is poisoned."}],"firstNight":12.33,"otherNight":25.33,"reminders":["Incorrect"],"setup":false,"firstNightReminder":"Show the Duende their question.","otherNightReminder":"You may show the Duende their question if it can be answered tonight. The Duende shows the signals needed to answer it. If correct, show them the ''You Are'' card, a thumbs down, and then the Grimoire for as long as they need.","art":"art/duende.png","jsonId":"duende_scp_fragmented_veil","curata":false}' WHERE slug='duende';
